  "findings": {
    "FINDINGS_TRAFFIC_HTML": "## Traffic\n- Sessions held steady month over month at **71K**, with mobile continuing to close the gap on desktop (44% of sessions vs. 38% a year ago).\n- The 18th saw a traffic spike (+22% over the trailing 7-day average) tied to a marketing push — no corresponding error-rate increase.\n- Weekday traffic outpaces weekends by roughly 2:1, consistent with prior months.\n",
    "FINDINGS_CWV_HTML": "## Core Web Vitals\n- LCP p75 improved to 2.6s (from 2.9s last month), driven by the hero-image lazy-load fix shipped March 4.\n- INP remains **Needs Improvement** on mobile (p75 380ms) — largely checkout-flow interaction handlers; see Top Pages.\n- CLS is healthy across both device types (p75 0.04), no regressions this period.\n",
    "FINDINGS_PAGES_HTML": "## Pages\n- `/checkout` is the highest-traffic page and also the slowest to respond to input (INP p75 340ms) — recommend prioritizing this for the INP fix.\n- `/product/[id]` pages carry the most exceptions (6 per 10K sessions), concentrated in the image-gallery component.\n- `/home` remains the fastest and most stable top page this month.\n",
    "FINDINGS_ERRORS_HTML": "## Errors\n- JS error rate held flat around 0.4% of sessions.\n- Request error rate ticked up mid-month (peak 2.1% on the 15th) tied to a payment-gateway timeout window; resolved same day.\n- `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined` remains the top exception by volume, unchanged from last month.\n"
  },
